WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:23.123
Brooklyn glanced nervously at the scoreboard in the gym as the seconds ticked away: 58-58.

2
00:00:23.124 --> 00:00:26.616
"Fifteen seconds left in the game," she thought.

3
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:33.959
Stuart had managed to steal the ball from the Terriers player who'd been racing downcourt.

4
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:44.962
Now he was dribbling toward the center court line, frantically looking among the players for an opening—probably hoping to pass the ball to Dirk.

5
00:00:44.963 --> 00:00:53.448
Just then the Terriers point guard lunged at Stuart. Brooklyn shouted, "Now, Stuart! Pass it!"

6
00:00:53.449 --> 00:01:02.354
Stuart released the ball. Dirk leaped into the air to catch it and zipped toward the basket.

7
00:01:02.355 --> 00:01:04.871
"Go, Dirk!" Brooklyn shouted.

8
00:01:04.872 --> 00:01:08.916
"Three seconds on the clock!" yelled Marv.

9
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:18.013
Dirk stopped near the basket. Then he spun and sprang upward, just as he and Brooklyn had practiced.

10
00:01:18.014 --> 00:01:30.502
The basketball sailed high over the players and then teetered around the basket's rim. Finally it whooshed through the hoop.

11
00:01:30.503 --> 00:01:38.672
"Yes!" Brooklyn cried. Whales 60. Terriers 58.

12
00:01:38.673 --> 00:01:45.298
The final buzzer blared. The Whales players surrounded Dirk and lifted him high in the air.

13
00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:53.417
"We're number one!" shouted Brooklyn, giving Marv a high-five. "League champions!"

14
00:01:53.418 --> 00:01:58.145
"Woo-hoo!" Marv cried. "What a coaching staff!"

15
00:01:58.146 --> 00:02:03.977
Marv put Coach Teagan on speakerphone so he could hear the news straight from the team.

16
00:02:03.978 --> 00:02:07.861
"We won!" the players shouted.

17
00:02:07.862 --> 00:02:12.869
"Way to go, team!" Coach said. "I'll see you at the team party!"

18
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:18.667
Brooklyn jumped around the court with the team and their happy families.

19
00:02:18.668 --> 00:02:21.880
"Great job, Brooklyn," her dad said.

20
00:02:21.881 --> 00:02:27.553
"Fantastic coaching," her mother chimed in. "We're very proud of you."

21
00:02:27.554 --> 00:02:32.273
Brooklyn grinned. "It was such an awesome game."

22
00:02:32.274 --> 00:02:42.935
Marv came up to Brooklyn again. "I know it was tough coaching your friends," he said, "but you handled it really well, Brooklyn."

23
00:02:42.936 --> 00:02:48.775
"Thanks," Brooklyn said softly. "Though Jacey might not agree with you."

24
00:02:48.776 --> 00:02:51.956
"What do you mean?" Brooklyn's mom asked.

25
00:02:51.957 --> 00:02:59.096
Brooklyn blurted out the story about the notes and the sign in the gym. Her parents were shocked.

26
00:02:59.097 --> 00:03:05.087
"Oh, honey," murmured Mrs. Robbins. "That's awful."

27
00:03:05.088 --> 00:03:10.251
Marv looked grim. "The principal is meeting with Jacey right now.

28
00:03:10.252 --> 00:03:17.250
She will have to sit out next basketball season. Neither the school nor the team will tolerate bullying."

29
00:03:17.251 --> 00:03:28.246
The Whales started gathering their basketball gear. Then everyone headed to Brooklyn's house for the party.

30
00:03:28.247 --> 00:03:31.966
"Whoa! That's some cake!" Dirk burst out.

31
00:03:31.967 --> 00:03:34.896
Brooklyn beamed.

32
00:03:34.897 --> 00:03:41.728
The big orange cake, shaped like a basketball, sat on a platter in the center of the dining room table.

33
00:03:41.729 --> 00:03:50.372
On top of the cake was a huge whale made of blue frosting. "Mom and I made it this morning!" she said proudly.

34
00:03:50.373 --> 00:04:03.782
Soon Coach Teagan and his wife arrived, rolling in a large stroller. Three tiny babies lay inside.

35
00:04:03.783 --> 00:04:10.352
While everybody gushed over the cute babies, Brooklyn ran upstairs to get something.

36
00:04:10.353 --> 00:04:17.861
"I hope the triplets like basketball." She gave Coach and his wife three small plush orange basketballs.

37
00:04:17.862 --> 00:04:25.565
Mrs. Teagan placed a ball next to each infant. "In this family everybody loves basketball!"

38
00:04:25.566 --> 00:04:29.596
The team ate pizza and reviewed the championship game.

39
00:04:29.597 --> 00:04:35.464
"That was an unbelievable pass, Stuart," Marv said. "Perfect timing."

40
00:04:35.465 --> 00:04:41.425
Stuart shrugged and looked at Brooklyn. "I just followed the assistant coach's instructions."

41
00:04:41.426 --> 00:04:46.591
"Me too," added Dirk. "She's the one who taught me the Jedi Jump."

42
00:04:46.592 --> 00:04:52.994
Brooklyn felt a surge of pride. "It's easy to be a good coach when you've got great players!"

43
00:04:52.995 --> 00:05:00.485
The team watched a slide show of photos from the Whales' season that Brooklyn's dad had made on his computer.

44
00:05:00.486 --> 00:05:05.325
Mrs. Robbins stood up. "Time to cut the cake!"

45
00:05:05.326 --> 00:05:21.398
Just then the doorbell rang. "I'll get it," called Brooklyn's dad. "Oh hello, Jacey," Brooklyn heard him say, sounding surprised.

46
00:05:21.399 --> 00:05:27.524
Everyone instantly fell silent. Jacey stood awkwardly in the doorway for a moment.

47
00:05:27.525 --> 00:05:31.868
"Come in," Mr. Robbins said quietly.

48
00:05:31.869 --> 00:05:37.390
"Jacey, we're sorry you chose to miss the second half of the game," Marv said.

49
00:05:37.391 --> 00:05:43.779
Jacey looked down at her feet. "I'm sorry I missed it too," she said in a small voice.

50
00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:51.127
"But I'm glad the Whales won." She raised her eyes to Brooklyn. "Can I talk to you? Outside?"

51
00:05:51.128 --> 00:06:02.775
"Sure." Brooklyn put down her plate of uneaten cake and went outside with Jacey.

52
00:06:02.776 --> 00:06:06.854
The girls stood together on the front porch.

53
00:06:06.855 --> 00:06:17.249
"I have to tell you the truth." Jacey had tears in her eyes. "I did it. I wrote those notes. Brooklyn, I'm so sorry!"

54
00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:24.752
Brooklyn stared at her friend. "I still can't believe it," she said. "Why would you do that to me?"

55
00:06:24.753 --> 00:06:30.077
"I was jealous. I used to be a starter on the team," Jacey said.

56
00:06:30.078 --> 00:06:37.588
"But then Coach and Marv started leaving me on the bench sometimes. Plus, you were getting all of the attention."

57
00:06:37.589 --> 00:06:42.325
"Huh?" Brooklyn furrowed her brow. "What attention?"

58
00:06:42.326 --> 00:06:48.816
"From Marv and from the team. Dirk too." Jacey's face turned red.

59
00:06:48.817 --> 00:06:52.713
"I think he likes you better than he likes me."

60
00:06:52.714 --> 00:07:00.145
"I just wanted to help Marv and the team," Brooklyn said. "I can't play basketball like you can, Jacey.

61
00:07:00.146 --> 00:07:04.721
I know I'm not a very good coach yet, but I'll keep working on it."

62
00:07:04.722 --> 00:07:12.213
"You're already a good coach, Brooklyn. Marv knows it. Dirk knows it." Jacey smiled sadly.

63
00:07:12.214 --> 00:07:19.053
"I know it too. You'll definitely coach in the pro league someday. I'm sure of it."

64
00:07:19.054 --> 00:07:22.955
There was a pause as the two girls looked at each other.

65
00:07:22.956 --> 00:07:34.284
Jacey let out a sigh. "I'm so sorry for hurting you, Brooklyn. Writing those notes was a stupid and mean thing to do. Will you forgive me?"

66
00:07:34.285 --> 00:07:40.942
Brooklyn nodded slowly. "I think so," she replied. Then she shrugged.

67
00:07:40.943 --> 00:07:46.259
"Who knows. Maybe you'll even play on my pro team someday!"

68
00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:54.273
"Maybe." Jacey grinned. "Only if you teach me that Jedi Jump. I heard everyone talking about it."

69
00:07:54.274 --> 00:08:00.597
"Sure. I'll show you how to do it right now. Let's get a basketball."

70
00:08:00.598 --> 00:08:10.662
Brooklyn rushed forward—and stumbled over her own feet. Jacey grabbed Brooklyn's arm before Brooklyn toppled down the steps.

71
00:08:10.663 --> 00:08:15.686
"Whew! You saved me!" Brooklyn said. "Thanks, Jacey."

72
00:08:15.687 --> 00:08:19.990
"It was the least I could do," Jacey said softly.

73
00:08:19.991 --> 00:08:29.501
The girls began shooting hoops in the driveway, and soon the rest of the Whales came outside and joined them.

74
00:08:29.502 --> 00:08:34.332
A few of them glanced uncertainly between Jacey and Brooklyn.

75
00:08:34.333 --> 00:08:38.208
"Everything okay?" Dirk asked Brooklyn quietly.

76
00:08:38.209 --> 00:08:46.146
Brooklyn nodded and dribbled toward the basket. She missed an easy shot.

77
00:08:46.147 --> 00:08:52.891
Dirk grabbed the rebound and passed the ball back to her. "Try again."

78
00:08:52.892 --> 00:09:02.059
Brooklyn dribbled fast. "Come on, Robbins," she coached herself. "Aim with your arms!"

79
00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:09.780
She lined up for another throw. Whoosh! The basketball dropped neatly through the net.

80
00:09:09.781 --> 00:09:13.119
Then Brooklyn heard another "whoosh."

81
00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:27.246
This time it was her team, cheering loudly for her. "Whales Whoosh!" they cried together.
